Description: ScreenR finds the genes that are depleted or enriched in
            pooled loss-of-function screens performed with barcoded shRNA or
            CRISPR-Cas9 sgRNA libraries, comparing a treatment with a control
            or the time points of a dropout screen. Gene-level tests based on
            edgeR and limma (FRY, ROAST, CAMERA, a Z-score test with an
            empirical null, tests across time points) give every gene a
            p-value and a false discovery rate. ScreenR includes quality
            control, the evaluation of CRISPR screens with essential and
            non-essential reference genes, the correction of the CRISPR-Cas9
            copy-number bias with CRISPRcleanR, and plots to check each hit
            at the level of its barcodes.
